<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39518" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmo</span></b> , ōnis, m.
		kindr. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλεύμων</span>, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεύμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a lung;</i> and in
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmones,</span>”
				<i>the two lobes of the lungs</i>, <i>the lungs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 55, 136</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				37, 72, § 188</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Curc. 2, 1, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9, 201</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. P. 1,
				3, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 3, 27</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Very important in haruspicy,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 39, 85</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 12, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
			622</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 548</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a marine
			animal</i>, <i>a sea-lung</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 47,
				71, § 154</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 35, 85, §
			359</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 9, 32,
				§ 102</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, in allusion to its dulness: pulmon'es,
					qui perhibetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 5, 1, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
